On commas as indicating pauses: while commas _sometimes_ function to
indicate a pause, they do not always do so. A comma would be correct
here, even though you wouldn't necessarily hear one out loud (though
I'd argue you _would_; "Good day, Master!" sounds different from "Good
day Master!", which latter makes me wonder what exactly a day-master
is). For more on commas and their uses and misuses, I'd recommend the
excellent _Eats, Shoots, and Leaves_, by some British lady whose name
I've forgotten.



